§3 concluded the guest's USERD address cannot be had, from a true premise about the INTERFACE
("named by handle+offset, never by a VA") carried into a false conclusion about the
INFORMATION. The guest's CPU-RM resolves the handle LOCALLY BEFORE THE RPC -- GSP has no
client-handle namespace to look one up in -- and ships the PHYSICAL address in the same buffer
the handle comes out of. NV_CHANNEL_ALLOC_PARAMS carries userdMem beside hUserdMemory[0], and
the Rust port already parses it as kayfabe_core::rmgraph::DeclaredUserd.

★ And there was never a page-table path to point at: ogkm programs the instance block from
memdescGetPhysAddr(pUserdSubDeviceMemDesc, AT_GPU, 0), a PHYSICAL address, 4 KiB-attributed,
which never touches PT*/PD*.

⊘ Two sibling docs reached the same wrong conclusion from the same premise and are corrected in
the kayfabe tree: leg_b_userd_adoption_blocker.md §1 and traces/boots/w262/RESULT.md §5.

